//! VeriFe: prove a field of any post-Capella execution payload from one
//! EIP-4788 beacon block root.
//!
//! This ingot holds all of the proof logic and nothing else: no storage, no
//! I/O, and no anchor source. The EVM verifier (`contract`) and the native CLI
//! (`cli`) are thin shells over it that differ only in where the anchor root
//! and SHA-256 come from.
//!
//! Module map (see `docs/architecture.md`):
//!
//! | Module     | Responsibility                                          |
//! | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
//! | `gindex`   | `const fn` generalized-index math: depth, concat, bounds |
//! | `layout`   | one Fe type per fork's SSZ layout                        |
//! | `hash`     | the `Hasher` interface: precompile 0x02 or software      |
//! | `merkle`   | branch verification driven by a gindex                   |
//! | `header`   | `BeaconBlockHeader` hashing and field extraction         |
//! | `verify`   | the recent path and the historical path                  |
//! | `dispatch` | `Fork`, the boundary table, exhaustive `(anchor, target)` |
